            <div xml:id="d102">

                <pb facs="0106" n="96" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg96"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Portugal/1442: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-04T12:00:00+00:00">March 4,
                            1944—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 7:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>683. The British Ambassador saw the Secretary General of Foreign Office yesterday
                    in the matter of the temporary embargo on wolfram exports to Germany. According
                    to Campbell while Sampaio was not of course in a position to commit the
                    Portuguese Government to anything he was impressed though worried. Sampaio
                    indicated that Salazar had summoned for a meeting the chief officials concerned
                    with this question.</p>
                <p>I shall follow up this <hi rendition="#italic">démarche</hi> at the beginning of
                    next week by which time the matter should have been given full consideration by
                    the Portuguese Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
